{"label":"[D]","input_label":"[D]","node":"unrealizable: The row sets an effective freeze of zero descendants on an already-active block and later clears it, restoring that block at height 102. At the pin a block's freeze is assigned when its own connection spends a consensus-frozen output. The duration setter rejects negatives but has no upper bound: literal zero maps to INT32_MAX, while nonzero int64 values narrow into an int32 field. On the pinned build's ordinary conversion, 4294967296 narrows to zero; the block is frozen but its child receives -1 and is not effectively frozen. This source-derived boundary is unmeasured. It does not supply the row's explicit set/clear route on an already-active block: no supported RPC clears the persisted block mark; clearing blacklist entries is a different operation. The declaration remains unchanged pending the captain's re-cut decision. [SRC] src/init.cpp:3340-3347; src/config.cpp:2602-2612; src/config.h:984; src/validation.cpp:3402-3407,3720-3740; src/block_index.h:548-557,576-580,1135-1140; src/disk_block_index.h:100-116; src/rpc/frozentxo_rpc.cpp:501-528 at 6504a3aff65ba97c0f6c80962b033e35ecbfed4b [X] docs/records/20261014-032012-s6-72-regtest-s3.md","source_pin":"6504a3aff65ba97c0f6c80962b033e35ecbfed4b","sources":["src/validation.cpp:3021-3719","src/processing_block_index.cpp:9-77","src/validation.cpp:4413-5330","src/txmempool.cpp:2330-2560"],"id":"chain-soft-freeze","case":"soft-freeze","expected":{"removed":{"height":101,"coins":["F"],"pool":["T"],"held":[]},"restored":{"height":102,"coins":["T"],"pool":[],"held":[]},"causeRecorded":true}}
